# Every byte here verbatim.
#
# The manifest is signed over its exact bytes. Git's newline conversion
# rewrote six carriage returns out of it on the way in, so what this repository
# served was six bytes shorter than what was signed and every install refused
# it -- reporting the manifest as unsigned, which is what tampering looks like.
#
# Nothing in this repository is source. There is nothing here that wants
# normalising, so the whole thing is exempt.
* -text
